    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/storage/mooncake_store/mooncake_store.py`:\n1. `MooncakeStore.__init__` accepts `storage_config: HiCacheStorageConfig = None` and guards `if storage_config is not None:` across every branch except `self.should_split_heads = storage_config.should_split_heads`, which raises `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'should_split_heads'` when `MooncakeStore()` is initialized with the default `storage_config=None`.\n2. In `standalone_storage` mode, `mem_pool.allocator` was accessed directly without guarding `mem_pool is None`, raising `AttributeError` instead of the descriptive `RuntimeError` when `mem_pool` is omitted.\n3. `MooncakeStoreConfig.from_file()` and `MooncakeStoreConfig.load_from_extra_config()` checked `\"master_server_address\" not in config and \"client_server_address\" not in config` (membership only), whereas `MooncakeBaseStore._load_config()` checks `extra_config.get(\"master_server_address\") is not None or extra_config.get(\"client_server_address\") is not None`. When serialized configs contain `{\"master_server_address\": None, \"client_server_address\": None}`, `load_from_extra_config` / `from_file` did not raise `ValueError`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Guard `self.should_split_heads = bool(storage_config is not None and storage_config.should_split_heads)`.\n- Check `if mem_pool is None or not isinstance(mem_pool.allocator, MooncakeHostTensorAllocator):` when validating `MooncakeHostTensorAllocator` in `standalone_storage` mode.\n- Check `.get(\"master_server_address\") is None and .get(\"client_server_address\") is None` in `from_file()` and `load_from_extra_config()`.\n- Add unit tests in `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_mooncake_ssd_offload_path.py`.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nCredit to @huangtingwei9988 (#18541), @xiezhq-hermann, and @alphabetc1 (#41343) for their foundational work on `MooncakeStore` and HiCache heterogeneous TP / hybrid pool support.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [